# Extended instrument taxonomy & temporal identifiers

Scoped rule for the Phase 1 (migrations 0039 + 0040) expansion of the
instrument polymorphic root, the temporal identifier resolver, and the
continuous futures-curve constructor.

Narrative walkthrough lives in
[aqp_docs/docs/concepts/platform/instrument-taxonomy.md](mdc:aqp_docs/docs/concepts/platform/instrument-taxonomy.md),
[aqp_docs/docs/concepts/platform/temporal-identifiers.md](mdc:aqp_docs/docs/concepts/platform/temporal-identifiers.md), and
[aqp_docs/docs/concepts/data/futures-curves.md](mdc:aqp_docs/docs/concepts/data/futures-curves.md).

## Hard rules

1. **Every new instrument subclass MUST set a unique
   ``polymorphic_identity``.** The string MUST match an
   :class:`aqp.core.domain.enums.InstrumentClass` value. Add the enum
   value first, then the SQL table, then the in-memory domain class.
   Existing identities: ``spot``, ``etf``, ``index``, ``bond``,
   ``future``, ``option``, ``fx_pair``, ``crypto_token``, ``cfd``,
   ``spot_commodity``, ``synthetic``, ``betting``, ``nft``, ``reit``,
   ``mutual_fund``, ``otc_derivative``, ``adr``, ``gdr``.

2. **In-memory domain classes self-register via
   ``@register_instrument_class(asset_class, instrument_class)``.**
   Decorate the dataclass; don't call the registry manually. The
   ``(asset_class, instrument_class)`` pair MUST be unique;
   double-registration raises at import time.

3. **ADR / GDR rows carry a FK back to the underlying.** Both
   :class:`aqp.persistence.models_instruments.InstrumentADR` and
   :class:`InstrumentGDR` have ``underlying_instrument_id`` pointing at
   ``instruments.id``. Never re-purpose ``InstrumentEquity.is_adr`` as
   the primary discriminator -- use the dedicated subclass row. The
   ``is_adr`` flag on InstrumentEquity is back-compat only.

4. **Identifier resolution flows through
   :class:`aqp.data.identity.IdentifierResolver`.** Direct queries
   against ``identifier_links`` are forbidden in agent / pipeline /
   strategy code. New entity kinds extend the resolver, not the
   callers. The legacy ``Instrument.identifiers`` JSON blob is kept
   for backward compatibility but is no longer authoritative; migration
   0040 backfills it into ``identifier_links``.

5. **Agent reads of measure / depositary-receipt / REIT metadata go
   through the DataMCP tools.** Specifically
   ``data.instruments.measures``,
   ``data.instruments.depositary_receipts``,
   ``data.instruments.reit_portfolio``. Don't ``from aqp.persistence
   import InstrumentREIT`` inside agent / tool code (AGENTS rule 22).

6. **Option chain payloads transit via
   :class:`aqp.core.domain.options.OptionChainPayload`.** Both columnar
   and record forms are accepted on input; the serializer emits record
   form. Don't ship raw columnar dicts across an MCP / REST boundary --
   the OpenBB-flagged failure mode (mis-aligned column lengths silently
   dropping rows) only triggers when the boundary skips this validator.

7. **Continuous futures curves are stitched through
   :mod:`aqp.data.futures.curve`.** Three roll strategies are provided
   (volume, date, open_interest); three adjustment modes (none,
   back_adjusted, ratio). New roll rules subclass
   :class:`RollRule`; don't hand-roll a one-off stitching loop in the
   strategy module.

8. **New ``instrument_measures`` rows MUST carry a valid
   ``source_dataset_id`` whenever the measure lives in a registered
   dataset.** NULL is reserved for synthetic / computed measures
   (e.g. an MA-crossover signal). The composite unique key is
   ``(instrument_id, measure_type, frequency, dataset_field)`` -- two
   measures cannot occupy the same address.

## Cross-references

- AGENTS rule 1 (``Symbol.parse``) -- the legacy
  :class:`aqp.core.types.Symbol` still routes `vt_symbol` parsing.
- AGENTS rule 3 -- futures-curve Iceberg writes go through
  :func:`aqp.data.iceberg_catalog.append_arrow` with
  ``medallion_layer="gold"``.
- AGENTS rule 21 -- Gold-tier futures namespaces:
  ``aqp_gold_futures.continuous_curves``.
- AGENTS rule 22 -- Agent access via DataMCP tools, never ORM.
- AGENTS rule 33 -- ADR-underlying linkage emits an ownership-graph
  edge so multi-hop joins stay correct.
